{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <utility>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int n, m, mod;\n    cin >> n >> m >> mod;\n    \n    const int N = 510;\n    vector<vector<int>> C(N, vector<int>(N, 0));\n    vector<vector<pair<int, int>>> dp(N, vector<pair<int, int>>(N, {0, 0}));\n    \n    // Precompute binomial coefficients\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n        C[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j) {\n            C[i][j] = C[i-1][j] + C[i-1][j-1];\n            if (C[i][j] >= mod) C[i][j] -= mod;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    auto add = [&](int a, int b) -> int {\n        a += b;\n        if (a >= mod) a -= mod;\n        return a;\n    };\n    \n    auto mul_pair = [&](const pair<int, int>& a, const pair<int, int>& b) -> pair<int, int> {\n        long long f = (1LL * a.first * b.first) % mod;\n        long long s = (1LL * a.first * b.second + 1LL * a.second * b.first) % mod;\n        return {(int)f, (int)s};\n    };\n    \n    auto sum_range = [](int l, int r) -> int {\n        return (l + r) * (r - l + 1) / 2;\n    };\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n        dp[i][0] = {1, 0};\n        for (int j = 1; j <= min(i, m); ++j) {\n            if (i != j) {\n                for (int k = 1; k <= i; ++k) {\n                    auto term = mul_pair(mul_pair(dp[k-1][k-1], dp[i-k][j-k+1]), {C[j][k-1], 0});\n                    dp[i][j].first = add(dp[i][j].first, term.first);\n                    dp[i][j].second = add(dp[i][j].second, term.second);\n                }\n            } else {\n                for (int k = 1; k <= i; ++k) {\n                    int val = (i + 1) * (k * k - sum_range(1, k) + sum_range(k+1, i) - k * (i - k));\n                    auto term = mul_pair(mul_pair(mul_pair(dp[k-1][k-1], dp[i-k][i-k]), {C[i-1][k-1], 0}), {val % mod, 0});\n                    dp[i][j].first = add(dp[i][j].first, term.first);\n                    dp[i][j].second = add(dp[i][j].second, term.second);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << dp[n][m].second << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    mod = int(data[2])\n    \n    N = 510\n    C = [[0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n    dp = [[[0, 0] for _ in range(N)] for _ in range(N)]\n    \n    # Precompute binomial coefficients\n    for i in range(N):\n        C[i][0] = 1\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            C[i][j] = C[i-1][j] + C[i-1][j-1]\n            if C[i][j] >= mod:\n                C[i][j] -= mod\n    \n    def add(a, b):\n        a += b\n        if a >= mod:\n            a -= mod\n        return a\n    \n    def mul_pair(a, b):\n        f = (a[0] * b[0]) % mod\n        s = (a[0] * b[1] + a[1] * b[0]) % mod\n        return [f, s]\n    \n    def sum_range(l, r):\n        return (l + r) * (r - l + 1) // 2\n    \n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        dp[i][0] = [1, 0]\n        for j in range(1, min(i, m) + 1):\n            if i != j:\n                for k in range(1, i + 1):\n                    term = mul_pair(mul_pair(dp[k-1][k-1], dp[i-k][j-k+1]), [C[j][k-1], 0])\n                    dp[i][j][0] = add(dp[i][j][0], term[0])\n                    dp[i][j][1] = add(dp[i][j][1], term[1])\n            else:\n                for k in range(1, i + 1):\n                    val = (i + 1) * (k * k - sum_range(1, k) + sum_range(k+1, i) - k * (i - k))\n                    term = mul_pair(mul_pair(mul_pair(dp[k-1][k-1], dp[i-k][i-k]), [C[i-1][k-1], 0]), [val % mod, 0])\n                    dp[i][j][0] = add(dp[i][j][0], term[0])\n                    dp[i][j][1] = add(dp[i][j][1], term[1])\n    \n    print(dp[n][m][1])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.60780744208023e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.03853429853916168, -9.810443589231e-05, -0.007620786316692829, -6.115249561844394e-05, -4.660974445869215e-05, -1.2278481335670222e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.6476224064826965, -0.005849030800163746, -1.1205610462639015e-05, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.17677053809165955, -0.000557267339900136, -5.8412379075889476e-06, -0.019467247650027275, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.06204290688037872, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -0.0008186326595023274, -1.8596476365928538e-05, -0.31326591968536377, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.0029841200448572636, -0.00010918975021922961, -3.933898824470816e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.9141146923357155e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0002975021197926253, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.3828182090946939e-05, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.00023183519078884274, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.4305104514278355